# Read by aquasecurity/trivy-action in the `images` CI job (.github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# Entries here are CVEs inside the Caddy binary bundled in the upstream
# `caddy:alpine` base image (frontend/Dockerfile, landing/Dockerfile,
# admin/Dockerfile). Trivy reports them as "fixed" because a fix exists in the
# library, but caddy:alpine has not been rebuilt with it yet. There is nothing
# to change on our side until upstream rebuilds. Remove each entry when a scan
# stops reporting it.
#
# 2026-11-13: caddy:alpine is now Caddy v2.11.9 (go1.27.3, go-jose 4.1.6,
# golang.org/x/net v0.60.0). It fixed all 5 older entries (CVE-2026-78667,
# CVE-2026-97031, CVE-2026-78669, CVE-2026-111943, CVE-2026-116587), so they
# were removed.
#
# CVE-2026-78661 (HIGH): golang.org/x/net/html denial of service through crafted
# HTML input. Installed v0.60.0, fixed in 0.62.0. Caddy `master` already uses
# x/net v0.62.0, but there is no Caddy release after v2.11.9 (2026-11-05) yet.
# Our Caddy only serves static files behind the edge proxy and does not parse
# HTML from users, so we judge the risk low (not verified in detail).
# FOLLOW-UP: when a new Caddy release appears, check
# `docker run --rm caddy:alpine caddy build-info | grep x/net`. If it shows
# v0.62.0 or newer, remove this entry. If upstream is more than about 2 weeks
# late again for a new CVE, plan a custom Caddy build (xcaddy) instead of more ignores.
CVE-2026-78661
